course: dictionary
lesson: 2162
title: Cornflour in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can mean one thing in one place and a little different thing in another. Cornflour is a thing you can touch, so it is a noun. The sentences give you clues: «a spoon of cornflour mixed with cold water thickens a sauce» tells you it is used in cooking to thicken things.
explain: Now read «Cornflour and water runs like a liquid when moved slowly but goes hard when punched quickly.» Cornflour is a powder, but mixed with water it behaves in a strange way. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then try your meaning in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Watch out for words that look alike. In the US, «corn flour» can mean flour ground from whole corn, which is a different thing. US recipes say «cornstarch» instead of cornflour, so if you see that word, it is the same kind of powder used for thickening.
fact: Cornflour is a fine white powder made from maize, which is another word for corn.
fact: «Cornflour» is used in cooking to make sauces, soups and gravy thicker.
fact: «Cornflour» is uncountable, so you say some cornflour, not two cornflours.
fact: In the US and Canada, the same powder is called «cornstarch».
fact: In the US, «corn flour» can mean flour ground from whole corn, which is different from cornflour.
exercise: What is cornflour made from? | Potatoes | Wheat | *Maize, which is another word for corn | Rice
exercise: A spoon of cornflour mixed with cold water does what to a sauce? | Makes it turn blue | *Thickens it | Turns it into ice | Makes it sweeter
exercise: A US recipe says «cornstarch». What is it? | *The same kind of powder as cornflour | A type of corn on the cob | A sugar sweet | Flour ground from whole corn
test: In science lessons, cornflour mixed with water makes «oobleck». What is oobleck? | A hard metal | *A strange slime that is hard when hit and runny when poured | A kind of bread | A sweet, sticky syrup
test: Gummy sweets are pressed into shapes in trays of cornflour. What is the cornflour doing there? | It is eaten with the sweets | It makes the sweets crunchy | It melts into syrup | *It helps shape the sweets, and the powder is sieved, dried and used again
exam: Jayden asks, «Is cornflour the same as corn flour?» What is the best answer? | Only in science lessons | *It depends where you are: in the UK cornflour is a thickener, but in the US «corn flour» can mean whole ground corn | No, cornflour is made from wheat | Yes, they are always exactly the same
